id: pm-jd3m6p
title: "PR #795 exact-head review hardening: dependency budget progress, rendered fixed points, nightly credential isolation, and drift-cache diagnostics"
description: "Exact-head bot review of PR #795 found that a context dependency request whose rendered envelope cannot fit even the minimum internal budget can repeat forever, rendered token metadata is settled with only two ad hoc passes, nightly checkout persists a credential it does not consume, and drift-cache root prevalidation maps permission or symlink failures to invalid_cache_path. The smoke gate also correctly caught the intentional activity help growth, so its versioned token-surface baseline must be remeasured rather than bypassed."
type: Issue
status: closed
priority: 1
tags[6]: "area:ci","area:graph","area:sdk",review-finding,security,token-efficiency
created_at: "2026-07-28T13:20:28.829Z"
updated_at: "2026-07-28T14:05:31.154Z"
closed_at: "2026-07-28T14:05:09.445Z"
author: "harness:codex"
acceptance_criteria: "A token budget smaller than the minimum context envelope terminates and returns the smallest disclosed result; Tree, graph, and context embedded rendered-token values reach a stable fixed point rather than relying on a fixed number of passes; Nightly checkout uses persist-credentials false and workflow contracts remain green; Drift-cache prevalidation distinguishes invalid paths from filesystem and unknown failures with tests; The activity token-surface baseline is intentionally regenerated and the smoke gate passes"
goal: project management = context management
objective: "Make the broad SDK/CLI delivery terminate deterministically, report exact rendered cost, and run scheduled verification with least privilege and stable diagnostics"
value: "A declared budget remains safe even when no representation can fit, while CI and diagnostics preserve their security and machine-readable contracts"
impact: Prevents an agent invocation from hanging indefinitely and closes exact-head review findings before merge
outcome: Unsatisfiable dependency budgets return the smallest disclosed result; rendered estimates settle to a fixed point; nightly checkout does not persist credentials; prevalidation failures retain stable categories; the intentional activity surface baseline is ratcheted
why_now: "These findings were produced by the required exact-head review round for PR #795 and block a green, trustworthy merge"
parent: pm-5t33or
severity: high
resolution: "Exact-head review findings resolved: dependency budgets now make strictly decreasing progress and return the smallest exact rendered packet at the structural floor; rendered token fields settle to a fixed point; nightly checkout does not persist credentials; drift-cache prevalidation preserves stable failure categories; the activity discovery ratchet reflects the intentional contract."
expected_result: "Every exact-head finding is fixed, regression-tested, linked to its source lineage, and verified by the full mandatory gate set"
actual_result: "The first exact-head review found a non-progressing budget loop, two-pass self-referential estimates, overbroad cache-path classification, retained checkout credentials, and an outdated intentional surface baseline"
component: SDK dependency rendering and CI hardening
regression: true
