comments[4]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-07-28T13:20:28.829Z","harness:codex","Duplicate check: searched all statuses for unsatisfiable dependency budget progress guards,rendered fixed points,nightly persisted checkout credentials,drift-cache prevalidation categories,and activity token-surface baselines. Existing items own the shipped primitives or broader programs; none owns this exact-head regression bundle,so this item links back to each canonical lineage."
  "2026-07-28T13:57:19.002Z","harness:codex","Verification note: first linked replay run test-local-mmb37rte-vjhq8l correctly recorded two harness-definition failures. Full coverage was invoked under the outer empty-schema PM sandbox, so repository ownership fixtures saw no canonical links even though the same package-owned coverage command had just passed 100/100/100/100 directly; the token surface link also named a nonexistent script. These are linked-test metadata defects, not product failures. Correcting the links to repository-context package-owned runners before rerun."
  "2026-07-28T14:02:27.581Z","harness:codex","Verification note: tracker-mode replay confirmed that a copied tracker also changes repository-root ownership expectations; the package-wide coverage command is therefore not a valid item-level linked test under the documented outer PM sandbox contract and has been removed from linked metadata. Direct package-owned execution remains authoritative and passed all 381 files / 6,451 tests at exact 100/100/100/100. The focused sandbox-safe linked suite passed. Searching all statuses for the broader nested-sandbox isolation gap before recording separate follow-up ownership."
  "2026-07-28T14:05:01.490Z","harness:codex","Evidence: exact-head remediation now guarantees strictly decreasing internal context budgets, returns the last exact rendered packet when the structural packer reaches its floor, and settles self-referential tree/graph/context token metadata to a decimal-width fixed point. Nightly checkout no longer persists credentials. Drift-cache root prevalidation preserves invalid-path, filesystem, and unknown categories. Focused sandbox-safe linked tests passed; token-surface linked gate passed 90 measured surfaces. Direct full coverage passed 381 files / 6,451 tests at exactly 44,859 statements, 31,950 branches, 9,174 functions, and 43,571 lines (100/100/100/100). pnpm lint, typecheck, quality:static, token budget negative control, SDK/package parity, SDK surface, entrypoint and transport gates passed. Security secret scan and pnpm high-severity audit are clean. Package-first acceptance exercised 88 commands; packed npx passed; an unrelated temporary npm/Bun consumer imported runDeps and PmClient from the SDK and executed the packed CLI through npm exec and bunx at version 2026.7.28, then the temporary root was removed."
learnings[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-07-28T14:05:02.451Z","harness:codex","A rendered budget loop must make progress structurally, not depend on a defensive branch: cap the next internal budget below the current budget and treat the packer's controlled structural-floor error as the terminal smallest packet. Exact self-referential size metadata should converge by decimal digit width rather than assume two render passes. Broad package coverage is not currently composition-safe as a pm-linked test because outer PM_PATH substitution changes repository-root ownership fixtures; pm-ay3l0p owns that separate nested-sandbox defect."
